# ============================================
# NOT USED BY THE CURRENT BUILD - read this first.
#
# The build context for src/NewVixSmart.Web/Dockerfile is the REPOSITORY ROOT in
# all three callers (docker-compose.yml, .github/workflows/ci.yml, and the
# manual `docker build -f src/NewVixSmart.Web/Dockerfile .`), because the
# Dockerfile copies global.json, Directory.Build.props and
# aspire/Vix.ServiceDefaults from the root. Docker only ever reads the
# .dockerignore at the root of the context, so this file has never applied to
# any image this repository builds.
#
# It is kept only as the rules a standalone build of this project would need, and
# it is deliberately kept in sync with the root .dockerignore so the two cannot
# drift into disagreeing about secrets. If you add a Dockerfile here that really
# does use this project as its own context, these are the rules it gets.
#
# Changes to secret handling must be made in BOTH files.
# ============================================

bin/
obj/
TestResults/
*.user
*.log
logs/
*.trx
*.coverage

# Never ship real credentials. appsettings.Development.json holds the
# development JWT signing key and the three seed passwords; the csproj already
# sets CopyToPublishDirectory="Never" for it, so it is never needed.
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.*.local.json
secrets.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pfx
*.p12

# Database dumps and live data files
*.bak
*.trn
*.mdf
*.ndf
*.ldf
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
backups/
